   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of the\nstate highway system as the \"Catholic War Veterans Memorial Highway\"",
    "basePrintNo": "S5834",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5834-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-o, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S5834\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the highway law, in relation to designating a portion of\nthe state highway system as the \"Catholic War Veterans Memorial Highway\"\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nRelates to the designation of the \"Catholic War Veterans Memorial High-\nway\".\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends the highway law by adding a new section 344-o to\ndesignate a portion of the state highway system as the \"Catholic War\nVeterans Memorial Highway\". Effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Catholic War Veterans of America, founded in 1935, is a Catholic-\nbased organization that has a long history of serving veterans and\nactive duty military members and their families. The organization has\nposts across the country, including one in New Windsor, which has a\npositive impact on our local community. One small way in which we can\nhonor their dedication and commitment to our country and our veterans is\nby designating a memorial highway in their name.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2021-2022: A10108, referred to Transportation\n\n2021-2022: A10108, Reported referred to rules\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
